WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.510
Every great stay begins with a key.

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.122
Most people have one.

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.543
Marc has six.

4
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.500
Meet Marc. Host. Hero. Towel folder.

5
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.466
He studied sustainable tourism in
Holland, and worked from Costa Rica to

6
00:00:26.486 --> 00:00:27.480
Japan.

7
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.940
Then he came home, and
mastered the towel swan.

8
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.500
In Barcelona, two flats.

9
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.100
Bruc sleeps twelve.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.780
That is a football team,
plus a substitute.

11
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.800
It even has a PlayStation 3.

12
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.370
Then, the train to Sitges.

13
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.364
It runs on time.

14
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.960
Usually.

15
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.980
Marc is already there.

16
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.300
Four flats by the sea.

17
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.982
Poble Sec, Balmins, 2
de Mayo, Bonaventura.

18
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:07.600
Real light. Real terraces.
Real towels, folded by hand.

19
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.561
From ninety euros a night.

20
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.240
Six flats, two cities, one Marc.

21
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.800
Guests call him wonderful,
and super reactive.

22
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.092
He greets them in Barcelona and Sitges.

23
00:01:23.112 --> 00:01:25.030
Sometimes at the same time.

24
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.590
And 2027 is coming.

25
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:33.093
Carnival in February, a phone congress
in March, zombies in October.

26
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.950
So when you need a key,

27
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.058
you know who has six.

28
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.070
Merca Stay.

29
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.360
Your key to Barcelona and Sitges.

30
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.890
Book direct. Marc has the keys.
